/**
 * @addtogroup MIDILAR_SF_Clock
 * @brief Provides core timing utilities and clock abstraction for MIDILAR.
 *
 * The **Clock module** defines a set of lightweight and portable abstractions
 * for representing and managing time within the system.
 *
 * It separates:
 * - **Time representation** (ticks, frequency, and conversions)
 * - **Clock control** (hardware or software time sources)
 *
 * ### Components:
 * - @ref MIDILAR::SystemCore::Clock::Freq "Clock::Freq"
 *   Strongly-typed frequency representation in Hz.
 *
 * - @ref MIDILAR::SystemCore::Clock::TimePoint "Clock::TimePoint"
 *   Represents a timestamp with an associated frequency, allowing unit conversion.
 *
 * - @ref MIDILAR::SystemCore::Clock::Controller "Clock::Controller"
 *   Provides an interface for retrieving and managing system time via callbacks.
 *
 * ### Features:
 * - Header-only, lightweight design suitable for embedded systems.
 * - Strong typing for frequency and time representation.
 * - Supports multiple clock sources (hardware timers, software counters, etc.).
 * - Enables conversion between ticks and real-world time units.
 *
 * ### Usage:
 * @code
 * using namespace MIDILAR::SystemCore;
 *
 * Clock::Controller clock;
 *
 * clock.SetFrequency(16 * Clock::Freq::MHz);
 *
 * Clock::Tick now = clock.Now();
 *
 * Clock::TimePoint tp = clock.NowTimePoint();
 * float ms = tp.ToMilliseconds();
 * @endcode
 *
 * @note
 * The Clock module is independent of MIDI and can be reused for DSP,
 * scheduling, and general timing applications.
 */